cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use crimepy in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "crimepy: Accessible tools for downloading, combining, munging, analyzing, and plotting crime data"
abstract: >-
  A Python package that downloads the FBI's National Incident-Based
  Reporting System (NIBRS) master files for any year, turns them into flat
  tables for pandas, joins the segments of incidents, and analyzes and plots
  the results, built on amos for reproducible empirical research.
authors:
  - given-names: Corey Rayburn
    family-names: Yung
    email: coreyrayburnyung@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6524-9956"
version: 0.2.1
date-released: 2026-10-30
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/WithPrecedent/crimepy"
url: "https://WithPrecedent.github.io/crimepy"
keywords:
  - crime
  - criminology
  - empirical legal studies
  - fbi
  - nibrs
  - open science
  - reproducibility
  - uniform crime reporting
